{"packet_id":"D076-01","doc_id":"D076","jurisdiction":"San Diego, CA","category":"algorithmic_rent_setting","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Prohibition of Anti-Competitive Automated Rent Price-Fixing Ordinance","requirement":"Landlords may not use algorithmic devices to set rental rates or occupancy levels, and no person may sell, license or provide such devices to a landlord. Tenants may seek injunctive relief, damages or civil penalties up to $1,000 per violation.","key_value":"$1,000 per violation","coverage_conditions":"Residential rental property in the City of San Diego; applies to any person who sells, licenses or provides algorithmic devices and to landlords who use them.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"All residential rental property in the City; no unit-count or building-age limit stated."},"exemptions":"Software that publishes reports from aggregated nonpublic competitor data more than 90 days old, or from public information, and does not recommend future rates; software setting rates or income limits under local, state or federal affordable housing program guidelines.","penalty":"Tenant may seek injunctive relief, damages, or civil penalties up to $1,000 per violation; each month and each property is a separate violation; a prevailing tenant recovers costs and attorney's fees.","effective_date":null,"citation":"San Diego Mun. Code §§ 98.1101–98.1104","quoted_span":"(a) It is unlawful for a person to sell, license, or otherwise provide an
algorithmic device to a landlord.
(b) It is unlawful for a landlord to use an algorithmic device to set rental rates
or occupancy levels for residential rental property.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.9,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":"Effective date is the thirtieth day after final passage, but the packet leaves the final passage date blank."}
